invariant: INV-48
file: keccak_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: keccak_avx2_block reads every lane from state 0, so the bytes of
  states 1 to 3 are state 0's. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        uint64_t lane = s->lane[i][k];
--- new
        uint64_t lane = s->lane[i][0];
